# ---------- Third-party corpora: raw, large, regenerable, not ours ----
# python/MAST/ is the RAW MAST corpus as downloaded: 12,961 files,
# 1,209 MB, including PDFs, WAV, PNG screenshots and .pdb payloads that
# no result in this paper reads.  Section 5.8's evidence is the DERIVED
# op-records -- mast_oprecords/ and python/mast_oprecords/, both tracked
# -- together with python/mast_rates.json.  python/mast_adapter.py
# re-fetches the raw corpus from HuggingFace (mcemri/MAD, revision
# 5a82e32).  Ignore it BY NAME: do not restore a blanket `**/traces/`
# rule, which would also re-hide python/traces/ (Sections 5.2 and 5.4).
python/MAST/
python/MAD_*.json*
mac-consistency-replication/

# ---------- NOT IGNORED, DELIBERATELY ----------
# runs/                      Tables 3 and 4 (traces, results.txt, manifests)
# python/live_a1_*/          Table 6 (live LangGraph sessions)
# python/traces/             Sections 5.2 and 5.4 synthetic pilot
# python/oprecords/          Section 5.8 own-executor racy/sequential check
# python/dynamic_oprecords/  Section 5.8 topology dynamic confirmation
# python/hc_*/               Section 5.6 Finding 5 high-contention sweep
# python/langgraph_a6_*/     Section 5.12 ToolNode A6 reproduction
# python/cf_*.jsonl          Table 5 counterfactual re-prompts
# python/audit_sheet.csv     Section 5.9 blind sample
# mast_oprecords/            Section 5.8 corpus projection (DERIVED)
# baseline_runs/             Section 5.5 baseline comparison
# production_traces/         Section 5.7 cookbook study
# A published number whose data is not in this tree is a defect.  A
# directory in this tree that no published number reads is also a defect.
# check_tables.sh gates the first; REPRODUCE.md's map gates the second.
